---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { buildGraph } from '../lib/schema';
import { companyLine, publisherLine, site } from '../data/site';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/format';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'About', href: '/about/' },
];
const updated = new Date(`${site.policiesUpdated}T00:00:00.000Z`);
const description = 'Satsplain explains crypto from public sources. We plan to sell our own Safety Kit, and we say so. We do not claim personal investing expertise.';
---
<Base title="About · Satsplain" description={description} graph={buildGraph({ crumbs })}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="kicker">The desk</p>
    <h1>About Satsplain</h1>
    <p class="lede">We explain crypto for people who are new to it. We do not pretend to be the expert in the room.</p>
    <p>{companyLine}</p>
    <p class="meta">Updated <time datetime={site.policiesUpdated}>{formatDate(updated)}</time></p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="research-desk">Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      Satsplain is an independent editorial project. The name joins “sats,” the smallest unit of bitcoin, with “explain.” The audience is a complete beginner who wants to understand the topic before moving any money.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Satsplain Research Desk writes and edits the guides. The desk is not a registered investment adviser, broker-dealer, law firm, or tax practice. It does not hold customer funds and it does not place trades. Reading a page does not create a client relationship.
    </p>
    <p>
      Articles are researched and drafted with automated tools. A second pass fact-checks the draft against primary sources. The file must then pass an automated quality gate, including sources, citations, and the other checks described in the editorial policy, before it is published. Corrections are welcome on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      {publisherLine}. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Please do not send account numbers, seed phrases, or copies of an ID.
    </p>
    <h2 id="funding">How we are funded</h2>
    <p>
      No crypto company, exchange, or token project pays for coverage. We do not sell ads on the guides.
    </p>
    <p>
      Satsplain plans to sell its own <a href="/safety-kit/">Safety Kit</a>: a blank plate the buyer stamps with a seed phrase, a punch, a tamper-evident pouch, and a setup card. We have a financial interest in that kit. The Safety Kit page says so at the top, and any guide that mentions the kit says so beside the mention. The kit is not for sale yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      Editorial stays separate from that product. We choose topics because a beginner needs them. Guides cite their sources. No article requires a purchase. A paper backup of a seed phrase is a complete alternative, and the <a href="/articles/what-is-a-seed-phrase/">seed-phrase guide</a> says how to make one.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not use affiliate links today. If we add one, for example a link to a hardware-wallet maker, the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> will name the relationship before the link goes live, and the page where the link appears will say so next to the link. A fee would not change the sourcing standard.
    </p>
    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <p>We will not predict a price. We will not tell you that you should buy, sell, or hold a specific asset. We will not publish a guide that makes factual claims without links. We will not hide a correction.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> is the longer version of those rules. The <a href="/sourcing/">sourcing page</a> lists which documents we trust first.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
